WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.025
Check yourself with two questions.

2
00:00:02.025 --> 00:00:06.850
First: why does Step 1 assign the security
initiatives in do-not-enforce mode?

3
00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:11.892
The answer is b: to evaluate compliance
without enforcing the effect,

4
00:00:11.892 --> 00:00:17.288
until at least one evaluation cycle and
a compliance review with the I S S O.

5
00:00:17.288 --> 00:00:18.438
Step 9 enforces.

6
00:00:18.438 --> 00:00:21.238
Second: where does the
exposure register live?

7
00:00:21.238 --> 00:00:26.400
The answer is b, inside the boundary,
because it's a map of the attack surface.

8
00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.813
It never goes in a public repository.

9
00:00:28.813 --> 00:00:33.790
The module page has three more questions,
each linked to the unit that answers it.
